validateUser({ name: "Cara", email: "c@x.com", age: 16 });  // "User must be at least 18 years old"
```

## Notes / edge cases

- `!user.name` catches `undefined`, `null`, `""`, and `0` — but not whitespace-only strings like `"   "`. If you want to reject those too, use `!user.name?.trim()`.
- `user.age < 18` will be `false` if `age` is `undefined` (since `undefined < 18` is `false`), so a missing age passes. If age is required, add an explicit check:

```javascript
if (typeof user.age !== "number" || user.age < 18) {
  return "User must be at least 18 years old";
}
```

