## Notes

- **Rejection semantics:** out-of-range values throw `RangeError`; non-numeric or non-integer values throw `TypeError`. If you'd rather have a single error type for all invalid input, swap both throws for `RangeError` (or return `null`/`undefined` instead of throwing — just say the word).
